<speak>All right, Adeline. I will keep the papers together and wait for contact through the usual channels. I will not try to squeeze this into a casual conversation with someone else at the branch. Thank you for being straightforward about what you can and cannot address on the telephone. I should return to the office now; they have given me a good uninterrupted stretch, and I do not want to keep everyone waiting indefinitely. The diary and filing reminders can wait until I am home. Thank you for your time today, and goodbye.</speak>